  "scope": "One fixed physical asset represented by the proposed pair, relative to exactly the four existing physically inspected candidates. Metadata, actual byte binding and contract composition only. No image was viewed and no new visual judgment was made.",
  "reasons": [
    "The actual prior isolated pair observer positively identifies the same road using corresponding permanent landmarks, both original images, both terminal cross-sections and the complete approved road width. Its explicit same_asset/same_condition/distinct_captures conclusions bind current original hashes, exact target polygons, context, assignment, artifact and row hashes. This audit attributes that visual judgment to pair_verifier_3.",
    "Both observations retain the identical preregistered 30.43168374472548 m world scope and bounded target. All six complete-image envelopes independently recompute exactly from the current hashed extraction receipts and declared affine/CRS metadata. Existing source core reports bind matching current manifest, label, protocol, exposure and audit-code hashes, report all four derivatives verified in each branch, and show only grouping_not_verified for the proposed pair observations.",
    "All eight complete-image envelopes of the new observations versus the four established candidates are disjoint. Since each fixed observed target lies inside its complete image, this rules out fixed-target overlap with those four candidates without inventing visual cross-asset comparisons. Group IDs alone are not used as physical proof.",
    "Existing conservative site/event partitioning, parent-object capture batches and same-asset near-duplicate registration remain applicable. Exactly one primary and one repeat observation support at most one asset.",
    "D089 and the adopted UAV-derivative contract allow different parent objects and verified different author-date groups plus isolated visual pair evidence. They do not require fabricated flight IDs or exhaustive visual N-squared comparison. This evidence composition can document grouping for this one asset without lowering D089 or changing historical evidence."
  ],
